# build
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# what running the engine leaves behind, under whichever project it was run
# on. The console archive is a user file rather than a derived one, which is
# why it stays in the project's root and out of the derived directory: cargo
# clean should not take somebody's settings. Saved scenes are the same kind of
# thing and are there for the same reason. `.colby/` is what the engine derives
# for a project - the compiled assets - and `just clean` takes it. colby.png
# and colby.wav are what `just shot` and `just hear` write when nobody names a
# path, and they land wherever the command was run from.
settings.cfg
saves/
.colby/
/colby.png
/colby.wav

# mounts of projects that live elsewhere, made by the runtime so that their
# game crates are built in this workspace. @ref src/runtime/mount.rs. The one
# project that lives here for good is the Blank fixture, which is also what
# keeps the workspace's member glob matching something.
/projects/*
!/projects/blank/

# secrets and local overrides
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.cargo/credentials*

# coverage
*.profraw
/coverage
lcov.info

# profiling
*.mm_profdata
flamegraph.svg
perf.data*

# rustc crash dumps
rustc-ice-*

# patch and merge leftovers
*.orig
*.rej

# nix
/result*
